icci scalar"],["line","reference","Florides's cluster of uniform density, of the same mass and radius"]],"caption":["The Kretschmann scalar $K$ and the Ricci scalar $R^\\mu{}_\\mu$ of Einstein's cluster of constant speed against $r$ ($V = 1/2$, $R = 3\\,r_s$), the same at every $t$, $\\theta$, and $\\phi$, inside the cluster and in Schwarzschild's vacuum outside it, beside Florides's cluster of uniform density of the same mass and radius. Inside, $K = 35/(48r^4)$, which grows without bound toward the centre, where the density grows as $1/r^2$, and is $0.00900/r_s^4$ at the surface. Outside it is Schwarzschild's $12r_s^2/r^6$, which is $0.0165/r_s^4$ at $r = R$.","The Ricci scalar is $R^\\mu{}_\\mu = 8\\pi G(\\rho c^2 - 2p_\\perp)/c^4$, with no pressure along the radius and the pressure $p_\\perp = \\rho c^2V^2/2$ along the circles of the particles, so $R^\\mu{}_\\mu = 1/(4r^2)$ inside, which is $0.0278/r_s^2$ at the surface. Outside it vanishes. $R^\\mu{}_\\mu$ jumps at the surface, where the density falls to zero. $K$ jumps at the surface, where the density falls to zero."],"ricci_sentences":[[1,0],[1,1],[1,2]],"per_scalar":{"kretschmann":{"opening":"The Kretschmann scalar $K$ of Einstein's cluster of constant speed against $r$ ($V = 1/2$, $R = 3\\,r_s$), the same at every $t$, $\\theta$, and $\\phi$, inside the cluster and in Schwarzschild's vacuum outside it, beside Florides's cluster of uniform density of the same mass and radius.","clip":"We draw $K\\,r_s^4$ on a logarithmic scale from $10^{-5}$ to $10^{2}$, and cut each curve where it leaves its panel, as $K$ does inside $r = 0.292\\,r_s$.","legend":[["line","K","$K$, the Kretschmann scalar"],["line","reference","Florides's cluster of uniform density, of the same mass and radius"]]},"ricci_scalar":{"opening":"The Ricci scalar $R^\\mu{}_\\mu$ of Einstein's cluster of constant speed against $r$ ($V = 1/2$, $R = 3\\,r_s$), the same at every $t$, $\\theta$, and $\\phi$, inside the cluster and in Schwarzschild's va