{}_\\mu$, the Ricci scalar"],["line","reference","Einstein's cluster of constant speed, of the same mass and radius"]],"caption":["The Kretschmann scalar $K$ and the Ricci scalar $R^\\mu{}_\\mu$ of Florides's cluster of uniform density against $r$ ($R = 3\\,r_s$), the same at every $t$, $\\theta$, and $\\phi$, inside the cluster and in Schwarzschild's vacuum outside it, beside Einstein's cluster of constant speed of the same mass and radius. Inside, $K$ rises from $15r_s^2/R^6 = 0.0206/r_s^4$ at the centre to $0.0234/r_s^4$ at the surface. Outside it is Schwarzschild's $12r_s^2/r^6$, which is $0.0165/r_s^4$ at $r = R$.","The Ricci scalar is $R^\\mu{}_\\mu = 8\\pi G(\\rho c^2 - 2p_\\perp)/c^4$, with no pressure along the radius and the pressure $p_\\perp$ along the circles of the particles. It falls from $3r_s/R^3 = 0.111/r_s^2$ at the centre, where $p_\\perp = 0$, to $0.0833/r_s^2$ at the surface. Outside it vanishes. At the centre $K = 5(R^\\mu{}_\\mu)^2/3$. $R^\\mu{}_\\mu$ jumps at the surface, where the density falls to zero. $K$ jumps at the surface, where the density falls to zero."],"ricci_sentences":[[1,0],[1,1],[1,2],[1,4]],"per_scalar":{"kretschmann":{"opening":"The Kretschmann scalar $K$ of Florides's cluster of uniform density against $r$ ($R = 3\\,r_s$), the same at every $t$, $\\theta$, and $\\phi$, inside the cluster and in Schwarzschild's vacuum outside it, beside Einstein's cluster of constant speed of the same mass and radius.","clip":"We draw $K\\,r_s^4$ on a logarithmic scale from $10^{-5}$ to $10^{2}$, and cut each curve where it leaves its panel, as the $K$ of Einstein's cluster does inside $r = 0.292\\,r_s$.","legend":[["line","K","$K$, the Kretschmann scalar"],["line","reference","Einstein's cluster of constant speed, of the same mass and radius"]]},"ricci_scalar":{"opening":"The Ricci scalar $R^\\mu{}_\\mu$ of Florides's cluster of uniform density against $r$ ($R = 3\\,r_s$), the same at every $t$, $\\theta$, and $\\phi$, inside the cluster a