^{2\\Phi} = 1 - r_s/\\sqrt{r^2 + b^2}$, with $r_s$ the Schwarzschild radius of its whole mass and the core radius $b = 2\\,r_s$, so that $m \\to r_s/2$ far away and the fastest particles, near $r = 2.3\\,r_s$, move at $0.37\\,c$.","clip":"We draw $K\\,r_s^4$ on a logarithmic scale from $10^{-5}$ to $10^{2}$ and $R^\\mu{}_\\mu\\,r_s^2$ on one from $10^{-4}$ to $10$, and cut each curve where it leaves its panel, as Schwarzschild's $K$ does inside $r = 0.702\\,r_s$."}]}
